---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import portrait from "@assets/images/gianluigi-gasparetti-flute-sepia.jpg";
import DiscogsName from "@features/discography/components/DiscogsName.astro";
import { getOwnReleaseCount, getReleaseLinks } from "@features/discography/domain/releases";
import { externalLinks } from "@features/shared/config/site";
import ProsePage from "@features/shared/components/ProsePage.astro";
import ProseSection from "@features/shared/components/ProseSection.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@features/shared/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const releases = await getReleaseLinks([
  "static-soundscapes-three-lights-at-the-end-of-the-world",
  "the-spirals-of-time",
  "genesis",
  "the-path-of-white-clouds",
  "dreamfields",
  "the-martian-chronicles",
  "the-physics-of-heaven",
  "cloudlands",
  "il-silenzio-di-dio",
  "i-hear-the-wind-singing",
  "i-hear-the-woods-whispering",
]);
const ownReleaseCount = await getOwnReleaseCount();
const portraitAlt = "Sepia photo of Gianluigi Gasparetti seated on a rug, holding a wooden flute between two clay vessel drums";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Biography"
  description="The life and music of Gianluigi Gasparetti (1958–2013), known as Oöphoi: Deep Listenings magazine, his instruments, The Kiva studio and his collaborations."
  image={portrait}
  imageAlt={portraitAlt}
  type="profile"
>
  <ProsePage eyebrow="Gianluigi Gasparetti · 1958 – 2013" title="Biography">
    <figure slot="figure" class="flex w-full max-w-[248px] flex-col gap-3">
      <Image
        src={portrait}
        alt={portraitAlt}
        widths={[248, 496]}
        sizes="(min-width: 640px) 248px, 100vw"
        loading="eager"
        class="aspect-[248/400] w-full rounded-[2px] object-cover"
      />
      <figcaption class="text-[13px] text-muted">Gianluigi Gasparetti with a wooden flute.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <ProseSection id="life" title="Life and Deep Listenings">
      <p>
        Oöphoi was the pseudonym of Gianluigi Gasparetti, born in Rome, Italy, on 26 March 1958. A music collector
        since childhood, he was also the editor of <a href={externalLinks.deepListenings}><em>Deep Listenings</em></a>,
        an Italian magazine devoted to ambient and deep atmospheric music, where he published interviews with many
        renowned ambient artists, including Steve Roach and Michael Stearns.
      </p>
      <p>
        He began his own experiments in 1995 with basic equipment, exploring the shores of deep space ambient music.
        His first album,
        <a href={releases["static-soundscapes-three-lights-at-the-end-of-the-world"].href}><cite>Three Lights at the End of the World</cite></a>,
        composed in 1995, was released in 1996 by the Italian ambient artist <DiscogsName kind="artist" name="Alio Die" />
        on his own label, <DiscogsName kind="label" name="Hic Sunt Leones" />. Alio Die himself plays for one minute on
        one of its tracks. His double live album <a href={releases["the-spirals-of-time"].href}><cite>The Spirals of Time</cite></a>
        followed in 1998 on <DiscogsName kind="label" name="Aurora" />.
      </p>
      <p>
        Gianluigi Gasparetti died in 2013, aged 55, after a long illness. The <a href="/memorial/">memorial page</a>
        gathers the tributes that followed.
      </p>
    </ProseSection>

    <ProseSection id="music" title="The music and instruments">
      <p>
        His music is static, organic and minimal, with a solid, monolithic feel, often set in a meditative and
        spiritual context. His recordings unfold through slight harmonic variations.
      </p>
      <p>
        He worked mainly with synths and samplers, singing bowls, flutes, theremin, waterphone, processed voices and
        unusual percussion: wood chimes, stones, shells and crystal chimes.
      </p>
    </ProseSection>

    <ProseSection id="the-kiva" title="The Kiva studio">
      <p>
        All of his music was recorded with analog-only equipment in <DiscogsName kind="label" name="The Kiva" />, his
        studio, a former stable in a fifteenth-century stone country house in the hills of central Italy.
      </p>
      <p>The <a href="/gallery/">gallery</a> includes a photo of him in his studio.</p>
    </ProseSection>

    <ProseSection id="collaborations" title="Collaborations and labels">
      <p>
        In 2002 he founded the experimental ambient group <DiscogsName kind="artist" name="Nebula" /> with
        <DiscogsName kind="artist" name="Klaus Wiese" />, <DiscogsName kind="artist" name="Mauro Malgrande" />,
        <DiscogsName kind="artist" name="Lorenzo Pierobon" /> and <DiscogsName kind="artist" name="Tau Ceti" />, which
        released <a href={releases.genesis.href}><cite>Genesis</cite></a> (2002) and
        <a href={releases["the-path-of-white-clouds"].href}><cite>The Path of White Clouds</cite></a> (2003).
      </p>
      <p>
        This site lists {ownReleaseCount} of his albums, EPs and minialbums, released on many international labels,
        including <DiscogsName kind="label" name="Hic Sunt Leones" />, Amplexus,
        <DiscogsName kind="label" name="Hypnos" />, <DiscogsName kind="label" name="Nextera" />,
        <DiscogsName kind="label" name="Electroshock Records" />, Skean Dhu,
        <DiscogsName kind="label" name="Stella Maris" />, Aplaus and <DiscogsName kind="label" name="Mystery Sea" />.
        He also ran his own label, <a href="/labels/umbra/">Umbra</a>, devoted to the music of new Italian ambient
        artists, and its sublabel for EP-length releases, <a href="/labels/penumbra/">Penumbra</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        His later work included several collaborations:
        <a href={releases.dreamfields.href}><cite>Dreamfields</cite></a> with
        <DiscogsName kind="artist" name="Paul Vnuk Jr." /> (Nextera, 2011),
        <a href={releases["the-martian-chronicles"].href}><cite>The Martian Chronicles</cite></a> with
        <DiscogsName kind="artist" name="Seren Ffordd" /> (Hypnos, 2011),
        <a href={releases["the-physics-of-heaven"].href}><cite>The Physics of Heaven</cite></a> with
        <DiscogsName kind="artist" name="Ran Kirlian" /> (Altera Orbe, 2013), and
        <a href={releases.cloudlands.href}><cite>Cloudlands</cite></a> with the Italian guitarist
        <DiscogsName kind="artist" name="Enrico Coniglio" />, under the name Aqua Dorsa (Glacial Movements, 2009).
      </p>
      <p>
        His last solo releases were <a href={releases["il-silenzio-di-dio"].href}><cite>Il Silenzio di Dio</cite></a>
        (Databloem, 2011), and <a href={releases["i-hear-the-wind-singing"].href}><cite>I Hear the Wind Singing</cite></a>
        and <a href={releases["i-hear-the-woods-whispering"].href}><cite>I Hear the Woods Whispering</cite></a>, both
        released in 2013 on Practising Nature, a division of Databloem.
      </p>
    </ProseSection>
  </ProsePage>
</BaseLayout>
